---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, CONTROLLER, CONSENT_VERSION } from '../config';
// Retention numbers from public provider docs. Account settings and written confirmations are still launch-checklist items.
---
<Base title="Privacy: jrdev" description="What the jrdev newsletter and website collect, why, and how to delete it.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Version {CONSENT_VERSION}.</p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>{CONTROLLER}. Privacy requests: <!--email_off--><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a><!--/email_off-->.</p>

  <h2>What we collect when you subscribe</h2>
  <p>
    Your email address, the topics you ticked (if any), and two tags saying you signed up on this page and
    which version of this notice you saw. Buttondown, our newsletter provider, also records the signup,
    confirmation and unsubscribe dates, plus the IP address and referrer of your signup. Open and click
    tracking is off.
  </p>

  <h2>Why, and on what basis</h2>
  <p>
    To send you the newsletter, based on your consent: the click in the confirmation email. You can withdraw
    at any time with the unsubscribe link in every issue.
  </p>

  <h2>Who receives it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The project maintainer.</li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/gdpr-eu-compliance">Buttondown</a> and its listed subprocessors, as processors under <a href="https://marketing.buttondown.com/legal/data-processing-agreement">Buttondown's DPA</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Cloudflare, which hosts this site and sees standard request logs.</li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy">Plausible</a> (hosted in the EU), our analytics. It receives each page view:
      the address and referring page without their query strings, and your IP address and browser User-Agent. From those it derives
      approximate location (country, region, city), browser, operating system and device type, and a visitor hash that changes
      every day. It stores event and session records with those derived fields, not your raw IP address or User-Agent. We only
      see aggregate reports. Retention: no automatic limit while the site exists; we can delete this site's analytics data at any time.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Transfers outside the EU</h2>
  <p>
    We (Versari AI, LLC) and Buttondown are both in the US, so if you subscribe from the EU or UK, your data is processed in
    the US. Buttondown's DPA includes standard contractual clauses for its processing; ask us for a copy.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Unconfirmed sign-ups:</strong> Buttondown can send one reminder after 24 hours. With cleanup enabled, unconfirmed addresses leave the visible list after 30 days. Cleanup keeps a hidden record by default; permanent deletion needs a support request or an API delete.</li>
    <li><strong>After you unsubscribe:</strong> with cleanup enabled, the address leaves the visible list after 7 days. A hidden suppression record remains so you aren't added again by mistake. Public docs do not give an end date for that record; write to us to ask for permanent deletion.</li>
    <li><strong>Erasure on request:</strong> permanent deletion at Buttondown within 30 days of your request.</li>
    <li><strong>Provider backups:</strong> after permanent deletion, subscriber data may remain in Buttondown's database backups for up to 2 days; Plausible keeps encrypted service backups for 30 days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What can't be undone</h2>
  <p>Emails that were already sent, and backups until they expire.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to access, correct or erase your data, and withdraw consent, by writing to <!--email_off--><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a><!--/email_off-->. You can also complain to your data protection authority.
  </p>
</Base>
